  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc1400.html",
  "prefLabel": "Plc 1404.01 Statutory Qualifications for Licensure",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 1404.01 Statutory Qualifications for Licensure.\n\n(a) As required by RSA 326-J:5, I, to qualify for licensure under RSA 326-J and Plc 1400, an applicant shall:\n\n(1) Be at least 18 years of age;\n\n(2) Be of good moral character;\n\n(3) Subject to (b), below, successfully complete an academic program with a baccalaureate degree or higher from an accredited college or university with a major in therapeutic recreation or a major in recreation or leisure with an option in therapeutic recreation;\n\n(4) Successfully complete a period of field experience as defined by the NCTRC under the supervision of a CTRS approved by the educational institution where the applicant is meeting or has met applicable academic requirements; and\n\n(5) Successfully complete the proctored examination administered by the NCTRC.\n\n(b) Pursuant to RSA 326-J:5, III, the executive director shall grant initial licenses to recreational therapists who were certified by the NCTRC prior to July 1, 2007 and who hold an active CTRS credential, provided the individual:\n\n(1) Has maintained the credential for at least 3 years in the 5 years immediately preceding submitting an application; and\n\n(2) Has met the continuing competence requirements for license renewal in the 2 years prior to application.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Plc 1400) #13705, eff 8-1-23; ss by #14442, eff 1-26-26, EXPIRES 1-26-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc1400.html"
